<title>BELGIUM: Gevaert surges on Almanij/Cobepa deal.</title>
<headline>Gevaert surges on Almanij/Cobepa deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Belgian holding company Gevaert rose nearly 18 percent to a new (post-1994, six-for-one stock split) life high of 3,520 Belgian francs on news the company's assets were to be divided between the Almanij and Cobepa groups.</p>
<p>Under the complex transaction due to be carried out over the next three months, Gevaert shares will be split in two and shareholders will receive a &quot;new&quot; Gevaert share and a Cobepa share.</p>
<p>The new Gevaert shares can be swapped immediately or in three years into Almanij shares.</p>
<p>Both Almanij and Cobepa surged on news of the deal, which was announced Friday when the companies' shares were suspended, hence lifting the value of Gevaert.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
